Given the sets $A =$ {multiples of 3 less than 12}, $B =$ {integers between 4 and 8} and $C = \{4, 5, 7\}$, find:

(i) $A \cap B$;

(ii) $(A \cup B) \cap C$;

(iii) $(A \cap B) \cup C$.

answer:
Write each as an improper fraction, with common denominator 120:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\frac{7}{4} - \frac{17}{6} - \frac{19}{10} + \frac{39}{8} \\
&= \frac{210 - 340 - 228 + 585}{120} \\
&= \frac{227}{120} = 1\frac{107}{120}
\end{aligned}
$$

> [!answer]
> {{green:$1\dfrac{107}{120}$}}

